Vendored terminal emulator
==========================

The terminal page at /terminal draws a real terminal, and the code that
draws it is here rather than at a CDN: rota is usually served on a loopback
address with no route out, and a page that fetches its emulator from another
host is a page that breaks there and a third party that can change what runs
in front of somebody's shell. These files are embedded in the binary and
served by it, from this server's own origin and nowhere else.

Both packages are MIT. The licences are beside the code, as
LICENSE-xterm.txt and LICENSE-addon-fit.txt, and are served too.

What is here
------------

  @xterm/xterm      5.5.0   lib/xterm.js      -> xterm.js
                            css/xterm.css     -> xterm.css
                            LICENSE           -> LICENSE-xterm.txt
  @xterm/addon-fit  0.10.0  lib/addon-fit.js  -> addon-fit.js
                            LICENSE           -> LICENSE-addon-fit.txt

Nothing else from either tarball: no source maps (each file keeps its
sourceMappingURL comment, which resolves to nothing here and costs nothing
unless a browser's devtools are open), no TypeScript sources, no README.

The tarballs each answered their own sha512 from the registry's metadata for
that exact version:

  @xterm/xterm 5.5.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@xterm/xterm/-/xterm-5.5.0.tgz
    sha512-hqJHYaQb5OptNunnyAnkHyM8aCjZ1MEIDTQu1iIbbTD/xops91NB5yq1ZK/dC2JDbVWtF23zUtl9JE2NqwT87A==

  @xterm/addon-fit 0.10.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@xterm/addon-fit/-/addon-fit-0.10.0.tgz
    sha512-UFYkDm4HUahf2lnEyHvio51TNGiLK66mqP2JoATy7hRZeXaGMRDr00JiSF7m63vR5WKATF605yEggJKsw0JpMQ==

And every file here is its own SHA-256, which a Go test recomputes from what
is embedded, so none of this can be edited without a test saying so:

  addon-fit.js            bdaefa370b1bfc42ee88d46fe6072400902a4d4b2d45cd93438dda9b23c97089
  LICENSE-addon-fit.txt   e256f01188af527e4d06d21d06fbf785ae9c50d4b328bf03cbe0ba7f0aa4228f
  LICENSE-xterm.txt       b569f629d00f2626a8100df2a1798210535621e42164dfd426a6fe5aac7b0ccd
  xterm.css               ba8e6985669488981ccf40c0cefe3aba80722cb6c92de7ad628b0bd717faf2b6
  xterm.js                1f991ac3b4b283ebf96e60ae23a00a52765dd3a2e46fa6fdda9f1aab032f7495

To update
---------

1. Read the registry metadata and take that version's dist.integrity:
   curl -s https://registry.npmjs.org/@xterm/xterm | python3 -c \
     "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['versions']['<ver>']['dist'])"
2. Fetch the tarball and check it against that sha512 before opening it:
   curl -sO <tarball> && python3 -c "import base64,hashlib;\
     print(base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha512(open('<file>.tgz','rb').read()).digest()))"
3. Copy the five files above out of it, put the new versions, integrity
   strings and `shasum -a 256 *` output in this file, and paste the same
   sums into the table in api/assets_test.go.
